Subject: [PATCH] [mlir] Clone nested regions from a worklist

`Region::cloneInto` clones each region of each operation it copies by
calling itself, so cloning IR nested N deep takes N levels of native
stack: `Operation::clone`, the inliner and every pattern that copies an
operation with regions overflow the stack of a thread with a small one on
deeply nested IR.

A region is still cloned in two steps, its blocks and operations created
and mapped first and their operands set and regions cloned after, and a
nested region still in full when the operation holding it is reached in
the second step; that step now keeps its place in each region it is
inside on an explicit stack. Blocks, operations and mappings are created
in the order the recursion created them. A unit test clones a chain of
operations nested 10,000 deep on a thread with a 256 KiB stack.
---
